CORE
initial4.sv
--aiger --top main
^aag [0-9]+ 2 3 0 [0-9]+ 2 [1-9][0-9]*$
^([0-9]+) [0-9]+ \1$
^[0-9]+ 0 1$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
The initial-state constraints r == a and t == a relate latches to an
input, and are not reset values. r and t are uninitialised latches, and
an additional latch, which is 1 in the initial state only, enforces the
AIGER constraints that encode the initial-state constraints.
